+# Bug Assessment: Inventory is not enforced across carts, checkout, cancellation, and product availability
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00Z
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: critical
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+Merchants report incorrect stock updates: checkout often decrements no stock or the wrong product, cancellation never restores stock, carts and checkout can exceed inventory, and zero-stock products remain available. The ticket defines atomic 409 Conflict behavior for cart changes and checkout, one-time restoration on cancellation, and quantity-aware v2 availability.
+
+## Symptom
+
+Stock is not treated as the product quantity exposed by `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}`. Checkout can create orders without sufficient stock and mutates unrelated availability rows; cart changes accept quantities above stock; cancellation is not inventory-aware; and product availability ignores zero quantity.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create products with distinct SKUs and quantities, add multiple products to a cart, and POST either checkout endpoint; observe missing or incorrect decrements.
+2. Add or update a cart item to a quantity greater than its product quantity, including a multi-update; observe that the cart is accepted instead of returning 409.
+3. Set an order to `CANCELED`, repeat the request, then attempt another status; observe no stock restoration/idempotency enforcement.
+4. Retrieve a product with quantity zero through v2; observe `available`/`canBePurchased` remain true.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java:180-220` — checkout decrements every availability and logs insufficient inventory after payment/order creation.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java:583-680, 756-900` — cart add/update paths mutate quantities without inventory validation or atomic rollback.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:1620-1648` — status updates do not restore inventory or reject transitions from canceled.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductPopulator.java:120-123` — v2 output copies merchant availability without quantity-aware flags.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java:343-468` and `ShoppingCartApi.java:70-165` — endpoint exception/status mapping must expose stock conflicts as 409.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+High confidence. Inventory mutation is implemented in the order service with the wrong product key (`OrderProduct.id` is not necessarily the catalog product id), loops over all availability records, and does not fail transactionally before payment/order persistence. Cart services do not share a stock guard, and status transitions are not coupled to inventory. Presentation maps merchant availability alone rather than the effective quantity.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Centralize effective stock lookup and guarded mutation around the product's default/all-regions availability. Validate the complete cart before any checkout side effect, then decrement only each ordered product's availability by its ordered quantity in the same transaction. Validate cart additions and all quantity updates before persistence, allowing only decreases/removals without a stock check. Introduce a typed conflict exception mapped to HTTP 409. On the first transition to `CANCELED`, restore each order product quantity exactly once; reject every later non-canceled transition. Make v2 `available` and `canBePurchased` the conjunction of merchant availability and positive stock, while preserving merchant-unavailable state.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/exception/RestErrorHandler.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java`
+- relevant cart/order/product integration tests under `sm-shop/src/test` and `sm-core/src/test`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+- Checkout multi-product exact decrement, wrong-product regression, insufficient-stock atomic 409, and both checkout endpoints.
+- Cart create/update/multi-update overstock rejection with unchanged cart, zero-stock add rejection, and allowed decreases/removals.
+- Cancellation restore once, repeated cancellation no-op, canceled transition rejection, and non-cancel status inventory invariance.
+- v2 quantity-aware availability and merchant-unavailable precedence.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Checkout must validate before payment and persistence, and transactions must roll back all stock mutations on failure.
+- Existing orders may have inconsistent order-product identifiers; use the catalog product reference/SKU, not the order-product row id.
+- Availability collections can contain regional rows; mutating all rows would reintroduce cross-product/over-decrement behavior, so use the same effective row exposed by inventory.
+- Concurrency can still oversell without database locking or optimistic versioning; preserve atomic service transactions and document any remaining limitation.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- None; the ticket specifies the required API behavior.
